{
    "background_story": "Zeke was a charming Southern baker with a passion for creating the flakiest, most tender biscuits in the county. Growing up in a small town, he learned the art of biscuit-making from his grandmother, who owned the local bakery. Zeke's biscuits quickly gained fame, with folks driving from miles around to taste his creations. He experimented with unique flavors, from sweet strawberry to savory cheddar and chive. Zeke's bakery became a staple in the community, not just for his mouthwatering biscuits, but for the warmth and hospitality he shared with every customer. On Sundays, he'd host 'Biscuit Sundays,' where the whole town would gather to savor his latest creations and swap stories. Zeke's love for biscuits brought people together, and his bakery remained the heart of the community.",
